    ],
    "description": "Natural Mineral Specimen\nSelenite Gypsum Crystal Slab on Matrix Rock\nRough Geological Specimen, Approximately 6.5 x 5 x 1.5 Inches\nThis natural geological specimen consists of a substantial plate of translucent crystalline selenite (gypsum) anchored to a sandy sedimentary rock matrix. Selenite crystal plates of this type form through evaporation in saline basins and exhibit distinct basal cleavage, glassy to pearly surface luster, and natural surface texturing. Specimens retaining their natural host rock provide valuable educational and aesthetic display value for mineral collectors.\nTranslucent crystalline gypsum (selenite) formation showing natural cleavage planes and surface pitting\nAdhering host matrix of tan and greenish sedimentary sandstone on the underside and outer edges\nNatural raw formation with fibrous crystal growth visible along perimeter margins\nMeasures approximately 6.5 inches long by 5 inches wide by 1.5 inches thick and weighs 2 lbs\nCondition:\nNatural geological specimen in rough, as-found condition. The crystalline face shows natural etchings, surface cleavage steps, and minor peripheral chipping typical of raw selenite. The sandy matrix base exhibits natural roughness, light particulate shedding, and mineral staining.\nThank you for all of your support!",
